WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:08.366
What SAY You!

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.333
This program puts the spotlight
on voice actors

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.666
who are active in various fields.

00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:18.966
We'll delve deep into their views
on their job and lives,

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.633
which you can't usually see,

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.366
in this documentary.

00:00:26.243 --> 00:00:29.233
Hello, everyone.
I'm voice actor Yuki Kaji.

00:00:49.766 --> 00:00:52.966
Looking forward to it.
I'm blushing.

00:00:57.333 --> 00:00:58.933
I don't really…

00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:04.600
Well, the viewers of anime, fans…

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.333
The chances of meeting them

00:01:08.433 --> 00:01:13.100
would be at anime events or stage plays.

00:01:13.866 --> 00:01:18.100
It's still difficult
to go to places like that.

00:01:18.166 --> 00:01:22.266
There are difficulties to overcome.

00:01:23.066 --> 00:01:27.666
So I want a chance or a place
to share entertainment.

00:01:27.733 --> 00:01:29.433
I hope we'll get them back.

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:32.633
So it's places like theaters or movie theaters.

00:01:33.233 --> 00:01:36.833
I hope we can go to those places soon
without worry.

00:01:38.866 --> 00:01:41.366
I hope life gets back to normal.

00:01:46.066 --> 00:01:47.800
You reserved a movie theater?

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:50.100
What amazing power.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.000
And I'm going there?

00:01:54.066 --> 00:01:55.866
Wow, I'd be happy to.

00:01:55.933 --> 00:01:57.933
-Let's go now.
-May I?

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.666
Thank you. I'm looking forward to it.

00:02:08.766 --> 00:02:10.033
This is impressive!

00:02:11.866 --> 00:02:14.633
It's a real movie theater!

00:02:15.666 --> 00:02:18.333
It's a luxury to be in this space.

00:02:19.166 --> 00:02:21.233
When there are stage greeting events…

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:25.800
Of course, I often come to theaters
as an audience member too.

00:02:27.466 --> 00:02:31.866
It's a bit lonely, empty like this!

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.566
Wow, this is the premium seat,

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.966
and the screen is very overwhelming
from this angle.

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.366
Excuse me.

00:02:46.316 --> 00:02:48.985
Well, this is a luxury.

00:02:48.985 --> 00:02:51.966
I think everyone gets excited

00:02:52.033 --> 00:02:55.166
when movies are about to start.

00:02:56.166 --> 00:03:00.733
I'm really feeling the anticipation.
I'm so excited.

00:03:04.833 --> 00:03:07.733
Well, there are many movies
I'd like to see.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:11.000
Needless to say, the ones I've acted in.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:16.700
But the movies that blew me away
as a child, and that I still love,

00:03:16.766 --> 00:03:20.033
are the Back to the Future films.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:29.759
As a voice actor, I'd like to
play the characters.

00:03:29.766 --> 00:03:33.496
They're characters that make me wish that.

00:03:33.496 --> 00:03:39.900
I'd be moved if I could watch
those movies in the theater.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.466
Is it possible?

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:49.846
It'll be so nice to watch them
in this great space.

00:03:49.866 --> 00:03:50.866
I'm so happy.

00:03:57.866 --> 00:03:58.933
Amazing!

00:03:59.833 --> 00:04:03.293
I've lost count how of many times
I've watched this at home.

00:04:03.793 --> 00:04:07.466
I was in third or fourth grade.

00:04:07.533 --> 00:04:10.200
For the first time, other kids and I

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:14.604
bought our own tickets
and went to watch a movie on our own.

00:04:14.604 --> 00:04:15.966
At that time,

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:19.100
Studio Ghibli's Princess Mononoke
was playing.

00:04:20.166 --> 00:04:21.100
And…

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:27.050
I watched it for the first time
on a big screen, in the front row.

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:28.866
It was so powerful,

00:04:28.933 --> 00:04:31.600
and my neck was tilting upwards like this.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.900
Talk about fear.

00:04:35.892 --> 00:04:39.633
Actually, there was some great timing.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:43.466
During the COVID-19 pandemic,

00:04:43.533 --> 00:04:48.433
we need to take necessary precautions
when we watch a movie in the theater.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:52.366
And as part of the plan
to get more people to watch movies,

00:04:52.433 --> 00:04:56.300
there was a revival of Ghibli movies.

00:04:56.646 --> 00:05:00.966
When I looked up whether any movie
would fit my schedule,

00:05:01.666 --> 00:05:06.900
Princess Mononoke was showing
at a time when I could go and watch.

00:05:07.257 --> 00:05:09.833
Watching Princess Mononoke in a theater…

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:14.433
It was the movie I'd seen
only with other children alone,

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:18.433
so watching it again like that
was a rare experience.

00:05:18.802 --> 00:05:21.566
And although in this year, 2020,

00:05:22.266 --> 00:05:24.666
the situation became like this,

00:05:24.733 --> 00:05:31.066
in terms of movies and theaters,
it was a great memory.

00:05:34.284 --> 00:05:39.566
I was often the leader of the pack.

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:47.097
I was the kind of child
who often played that kind of role.

00:05:47.097 --> 00:05:48.766
Apart from that,

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:55.933
as a child, I loved having dreams.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:00.710
I was a strange child
who liked working hard toward my dreams.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:03.700
Honestly, my dreams changed very often,

00:06:03.766 --> 00:06:07.600
but I wanted to give it my all

00:06:07.666 --> 00:06:10.933
when I did what I should do at the time.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.933
Then I started middle school.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:19.600
That was when I learned about a job
called "voice actor."

00:06:20.029 --> 00:06:24.033
I don't remember
whether it was on TV or in a magazine,

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:27.066
I've even forgotten who said it,

00:06:27.133 --> 00:06:29.233
but a very experienced voice actor said,

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:30.700
"Voice acting is a job

00:06:30.766 --> 00:06:35.145
where everything you work hard for
will become your strength."

00:06:35.145 --> 00:06:36.346
After hearing that,

00:06:36.346 --> 00:06:40.717
because I always worked hard

00:06:40.717 --> 00:06:43.019
to become a pro

00:06:43.019 --> 00:06:48.925
in what I was facing
and aiming to achieve,

00:06:48.933 --> 00:06:52.433
I felt that those words affirmed
what I did was right.

00:06:52.896 --> 00:06:57.333
Since hearing those words and
working toward becoming a voice actor,

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:03.300
the dreams I'd changed
as often as every two or three days

00:07:03.866 --> 00:07:07.143
turned into the dream
of becoming a voice actor alone.

00:07:07.433 --> 00:07:11.281
I then started high school
and entered training school,

00:07:11.281 --> 00:07:14.700
and I'm still doing this job now.

00:07:14.766 --> 00:07:18.266
So I think it really was
a fateful encounter.

00:07:22.192 --> 00:07:25.128
Well, it was incredible.

00:07:25.433 --> 00:07:31.300
That alone makes me realize
I was given a great opportunity.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.633
Somehow, this is sad, but...

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:41.478
I'm 35 now, but somehow…

00:07:42.633 --> 00:07:46.366
Five years ago, when I was 30 years old,

00:07:46.433 --> 00:07:50.200
I finally realized
what kind of person I was.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:53.333
Fellow actors I'm friends with

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:57.833
told me what I was like,

00:07:57.900 --> 00:08:02.966
so I found out what I was like
and how people saw me.

00:08:03.866 --> 00:08:08.833
I finally realized that
I'm more annoying than I thought I was.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:12.509
I'm a real pain in the neck
when it comes to various things.

00:08:12.509 --> 00:08:16.533
I'm sure that as long as I'm an actor,

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:19.516
I'm bound to have some peculiarities.

00:08:21.217 --> 00:08:23.766
Being annoying in a certain way

00:08:24.766 --> 00:08:27.300
is a kind of weapon, something that…

00:08:30.166 --> 00:08:31.566
makes you interesting.

00:08:33.033 --> 00:08:35.633
I think it's okay to have that.

00:08:36.266 --> 00:08:38.433
That's how I see myself.

00:08:44.466 --> 00:08:48.344
A famous fortune teller like him
read my fortune? Can I watch it?

00:08:49.746 --> 00:08:53.182
Thank you, Mr. Hoshi. I'll take a look.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.300
I'm Hoshi.
Let's get started.

00:08:55.366 --> 00:08:56.633
Please.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:58.421
I'm nervous.

00:08:58.421 --> 00:09:02.566
First, I'll look at Mr. Kaji's general luck.

00:09:02.633 --> 00:09:07.966
My first impression of his palm is that
he's a very nice person.

00:09:08.533 --> 00:09:10.934
-However…
-Wait, "however"?

00:09:10.934 --> 00:09:13.200
he's not just nice.

00:09:13.202 --> 00:09:17.273
His hidden strength
is shown on his left hand.

00:09:17.273 --> 00:09:20.233
There is a long, straight line here.

00:09:20.666 --> 00:09:22.845
It shows his ego.

00:09:22.866 --> 00:09:26.516
Something like his ego and belief.

00:09:26.516 --> 00:09:32.855
Perhaps what he shows people around him
is the gentle side,

00:09:32.855 --> 00:09:38.000
but he has a backbone, a strong ego
and a strong sense of responsibility.

00:09:38.828 --> 00:09:42.233
I can say he is hard-working.

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:44.366
This is one side of him.

00:09:45.366 --> 00:09:50.340
When I read Mr. Kaji's fortune,
I see his professional luck is strong.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:53.343
And this gradually spreads out,

00:09:53.343 --> 00:09:56.366
so probably various kinds of work…

00:09:56.433 --> 00:10:01.833
Maybe he will be offered work
besides voice acting.

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:05.154
Please try your best.

00:10:08.524 --> 00:10:11.060
It's close to what we were talking about earlier.

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:18.401
It matches what other people told me
and how I think about myself.

00:10:19.669 --> 00:10:21.000
Palm reading is amazing!

00:10:21.571 --> 00:10:24.841
And I'm happy that
he said I had good professional luck

00:10:24.866 --> 00:10:28.878
and I'd be offered new jobs.

00:10:28.878 --> 00:10:33.983
If given various opportunities,
I would like to try some new things.

00:10:33.983 --> 00:10:37.420
I really appreciate
his fortune telling.

00:10:40.256 --> 00:10:43.566
Next, we are honored
to have the presence of our guest,

00:10:43.633 --> 00:10:47.664
voice actor Mr. Yuki Kaji,
who will give us a speech.

00:10:51.768 --> 00:10:54.070
Hello, I am Yuki Kaji.

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:57.407
Congratulations
on the opening of EJ Anime Hotel.

00:10:58.207 --> 00:11:02.879
The scope of work as a voice actor,

00:11:02.879 --> 00:11:07.750
the variety of the content of our work,
is gradually broadening.

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:10.620
It's become that kind of era.

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:12.866
Personally, as a voice actor

00:11:12.933 --> 00:11:15.024
who acts with his voice,

00:11:15.024 --> 00:11:19.028
I want to see how much I can grow

00:11:19.028 --> 00:11:23.499
and use the experience I gained
to get feedback

00:11:23.499 --> 00:11:27.203
and make myself useful as a voice actor.

00:11:27.203 --> 00:11:28.433
That's what I think.

00:11:32.542 --> 00:11:39.282
In fact, I have been asked to
attend events overseas.

00:11:39.282 --> 00:11:43.319
The local people's passion about anime

00:11:43.319 --> 00:11:44.600
and about voice actors,

00:11:44.666 --> 00:11:48.591
I've had opportunities
to experience those things myself.

00:11:48.591 --> 00:11:52.628
Times are hard in the middle
of the COVID-19 pandemic.

00:11:52.633 --> 00:11:58.568
It has become quite difficult
to have such opportunities,

00:11:58.566 --> 00:12:02.538
but this is exactly when it's important

00:12:02.533 --> 00:12:10.246
to communicate with people
of various countries through anime.

00:12:10.279 --> 00:12:13.583
When everything gets back to normal
someday,

00:12:13.583 --> 00:12:16.619
I hope people overseas
will come to visit Japan,

00:12:16.619 --> 00:12:19.622
and I'd like to go to countries
all over the world

00:12:19.633 --> 00:12:24.827
to help and tell the people there
about the charm of anime.

00:12:28.464 --> 00:12:31.200
I'm fine. Thank you.

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:34.203
Here I am.
Let's go to the studio over there.

00:12:37.006 --> 00:12:41.410
Yes, I often come here
to do recording for video games.

00:12:44.881 --> 00:12:46.315
Hello.

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:52.288
I'm usually in the booth
so I don't normally come to this room.

00:12:52.288 --> 00:12:54.257
I'm nervous. Thanks for having me.

00:13:00.196 --> 00:13:02.732
When people watch anime or dubbed movies,

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:06.769
they feel at peace,

00:13:06.769 --> 00:13:10.940
or they gain the energy for tomorrow.

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:17.146
When I see reactions like that,

00:13:17.166 --> 00:13:21.884
I feel glad this is my job.

00:13:21.918 --> 00:13:25.154
The nephew of the makeup artist
who does makeup for me

00:13:25.154 --> 00:13:28.891
watches The Seven Deadly Sins.

00:13:28.891 --> 00:13:32.628
His dream for the future
is to become Meliodas,

00:13:32.628 --> 00:13:34.666
a character I play.

00:13:36.432 --> 00:13:40.069
When I heard he'd said that,

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:44.233
it reminded me of watching Dragon Ball
as a child

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:48.144
and wanting to become Goku.

00:13:48.144 --> 00:13:51.314
So, in a different way,

00:13:51.314 --> 00:13:54.050
this time, as a voice actor,

00:13:54.050 --> 00:13:58.054
I'm the one
who can deliver hopes and dreams,

00:13:58.054 --> 00:14:01.357
and I'm very glad to be a part of it.

00:14:05.795 --> 00:14:08.598
When I had vague anxiety about

00:14:08.598 --> 00:14:11.834
whether I could continue
doing this job or not…

00:14:13.603 --> 00:14:17.933
a senior said to me,
"You'll be okay. I'm sure of it."

00:14:19.942 --> 00:14:23.679
He kept telling me that.

00:14:23.679 --> 00:14:25.982
That word, "okay"…

00:14:27.416 --> 00:14:32.388
Of course the relationship between
who says it and hears it

00:14:32.388 --> 00:14:33.433
plays a big part,

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:36.692
but I think that word is very powerful.

00:14:37.727 --> 00:14:40.630
Even without any explanation,

00:14:40.633 --> 00:14:43.300
if this person says I'll be okay,

00:14:43.366 --> 00:14:47.169
then maybe I'll be okay.

00:14:47.169 --> 00:14:52.308
I think that word gave me courage
and reassured me.

00:14:52.575 --> 00:15:00.116
When my juniors are worried,
I say the same thing.

00:15:00.116 --> 00:15:07.924
Of course, I hope I can actually
give them advice on techniques.

00:15:07.924 --> 00:15:13.529
But I think the word "okay"
is very powerful,

00:15:13.529 --> 00:15:16.465
so I want to tell them that.

00:15:22.305 --> 00:15:25.074
Oh Mr. Kaji, it's Araki here.

00:15:25.808 --> 00:15:26.475
Director!

00:15:26.475 --> 00:15:31.681
-I've just talked a lot about you.
-Thank you.

00:15:31.681 --> 00:15:34.951
-I think I said something nice.
-You're confident.

00:15:34.951 --> 00:15:36.152
They were happy.

00:15:36.152 --> 00:15:41.123
I think you're doing the recording
for the next season of Attack on Titan.

00:15:41.123 --> 00:15:45.227
Regarding how you play Eren
in the final season,

00:15:45.227 --> 00:15:48.898
it's become quite a hot topic
of discussion among us,

00:15:48.898 --> 00:15:52.501
and I think the answer
you've been pondering for a long time

00:15:52.501 --> 00:15:54.203
must be exploding now.

00:15:54.203 --> 00:15:56.906
I'm looking forward to it.

00:15:56.906 --> 00:16:01.610
I'll be asking you to join my work soon.
Please wait for that.

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:04.513
-See you.
-Bye.

00:16:07.016 --> 00:16:08.517
Thank you.

00:16:09.051 --> 00:16:10.453
Thank you, Director Araki.

00:16:10.453 --> 00:16:12.121
I'm glad.

00:16:12.121 --> 00:16:17.259
The character really opened up
a new field for me as an actor.

00:16:17.259 --> 00:16:22.298
I couldn't be more grateful
for the opportunity to play him.

00:16:22.298 --> 00:16:27.403
If the day I can work with Mr. Araki
on something comes again,

00:16:27.403 --> 00:16:29.939
I will be very happy.

00:16:29.939 --> 00:16:31.674
Not just work, either.

00:16:31.674 --> 00:16:34.310
Let's go grab a drink soon.

00:16:34.310 --> 00:16:35.678
Thank you, director.

00:16:39.882 --> 00:16:43.853
First, he's very strict on himself
and very serious.

00:16:43.853 --> 00:16:48.891
I think he also does
lots of preparation work.

00:16:48.891 --> 00:16:52.294
He has as many as three, four jobs a day,

00:16:52.294 --> 00:16:57.366
so he must take quite some time,
a day or two before, to prepare for them.

00:16:57.366 --> 00:17:00.503
Anyway, he is ready when he goes to work.

00:17:00.536 --> 00:17:04.340
He is ready and we can feel his pride

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:07.276
when he is standing there.

00:17:07.276 --> 00:17:09.011
This has a good influence

00:17:09.011 --> 00:17:12.815
on the other voice actors at the studio.

00:17:12.815 --> 00:17:17.086
He only has to speak, and we all know
his presence is overwhelming.

00:17:17.086 --> 00:17:20.856
On Attack on Titan, this is natural
because he's the protagonist,

00:17:20.856 --> 00:17:24.260
but even when he isn't,
Mr. Kaji is still the leader.

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:28.497
We feel that this person
is the leader.

00:17:28.497 --> 00:17:31.901
That's how the atmosphere is.

00:17:31.901 --> 00:17:33.569
I don't mean he's intimidating.

00:17:33.569 --> 00:17:37.606
It's the difference in talent
among other living creatures.

00:17:37.606 --> 00:17:40.376
He only has to be there and we know.

00:17:40.376 --> 00:17:46.782
I feel that no matter where he goes,
he becomes the leader there.

00:17:46.782 --> 00:17:52.188
He is a serious person in nature.
A very serious person.

00:18:17.947 --> 00:18:18.981
Okay.

00:18:20.483 --> 00:18:23.686
Anime, video games,
stage plays, narration…

00:18:23.686 --> 00:18:26.622
The scope of work for voice actors
is now expanding…

00:18:27.690 --> 00:18:30.292
Well, I have nothing but dreams.

00:18:31.527 --> 00:18:33.295
I'm still immature,

00:18:33.295 --> 00:18:37.600
and there are many things
I'm not able to do yet.

00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:43.939
Of course, I want to do more and more
new performances and characters

00:18:43.939 --> 00:18:47.610
and play them wholeheartedly.

00:18:47.610 --> 00:18:49.478
That's all I want.

00:18:50.045 --> 00:18:52.081
Ever since I was little,

00:18:52.081 --> 00:18:58.621
my dream has been to give my voice
to the heroes of live action dramas.

00:19:00.623 --> 00:19:05.661
Like the movie I watched
at the theater today.

00:19:07.329 --> 00:19:14.203
My dream is that when people
think about a certain actor,

00:19:14.203 --> 00:19:16.272
and his voice in dubbed movies,

00:19:16.272 --> 00:19:18.374
they'll think of me.

00:19:18.374 --> 00:19:26.649
I hope someday I will have the chance
to be related to an actor like that.

00:19:27.082 --> 00:19:36.892
Also, I want to do each of the jobs
I'm given with sincerity.

00:19:36.892 --> 00:19:41.764
I'm grateful for the work I'm offered,

00:19:41.764 --> 00:19:43.666
and I feel it strongly

00:19:43.666 --> 00:19:46.769
after having experienced
the struggles of my early days.

00:19:47.002 --> 00:19:52.575
I'll never forget to be grateful
and will keep trying various new things.

00:19:56.212 --> 00:19:57.980
Thank you for having me.

00:19:57.980 --> 00:20:01.917
Wow, I've spoken a lot.

00:20:01.917 --> 00:20:06.222
I can't wait to see
what the program is like too.

